class Solution:
    def twoSum(self, nums, target):
        n = len(nums)
        for i in range(n):
            for j in range(i + 1, n):
                if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:
                    return [i, j]


EXPLANATION

The approach is to check each possible pair of numbers in the list. 
The first loop selects a number using i, while the second loop selects another number starting from i + 1, so each pair is checked only once. 
For every pair, their values are added and compared with the target. If the sum matches the target, the indices [i, j] are returned.
